From: LayerStream Opt-In Patch Overlay <layerstream@kleinbem.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] cuda: detect integrated UMA GPUs via cudaDeviceProp::integrated

Re-enables `cudaDeviceProp::integrated` detection for unified-memory CUDA
devices (e.g. Jetson Orin Nano / JetPack 7, DGX Spark) so llama.cpp can use
zero-copy `CUDA_Host` pinned unified buffers without doubling memory usage.

upstream: ggml-org/llama.cpp#15034
upstream: ggml-org/llama.cpp#16308

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
@@ -403,7 +403,7 @@ static ggml_cuda_device_info ggml_cuda_init() {
 
         info.default_tensor_split[id] = total_vram;
         total_vram += device_vram;
-        info.devices[id].integrated = false; // Temporarily disabled due to issues with corrupted output (e.g. #15034)
+        info.devices[id].integrated = prop.integrated;
         info.devices[id].nsm        = prop.multiProcessorCount;
         info.devices[id].smpb       = prop.sharedMemPerBlock;
         info.devices[id].warp_size  = prop.warpSize;
